# Windsurf Rules

This is a Vite + React 18 + TypeScript + Tailwind app. Low-end Android
devices common in Southeast Asia are first-class targets — performance
on constrained hardware is not late-stage polish.

**Canonical guidelines: [`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md). Read it before
non-trivial work.** Always-on rules:

- Animate only `transform` and `opacity`. Avoid `filter`, `box-shadow`,
  `border-radius`, `width`, `height`, `top`, `left` on animated paths.
- Throttle scroll/pointermove handlers with `requestAnimationFrame`;
  cancel on unmount.
- Debounce input/search/resize handlers.
- `backdrop-filter` is expensive — never on large surfaces. Use
  higher-opacity background instead.
- Lazy-load all routes via `React.lazy()` + `Suspense`. Per-route bundle
  budget: under 170 kB gzipped.
- Use semantic HTML (`<button>`, `<header>`, `<main>`, `<nav>`).
- Use `IntersectionObserver` and `ResizeObserver` over scroll/resize
  listeners.
- Set explicit `width`/`height` on media.
- Test at 375 / 768 / 1280 viewports; `useBreakpoint` hook exists.
- Clean up on unmount: listeners, timeouts, rAFs.

Budgets: TTI < 3.5s, LCP < 2.5s, INP < 200ms, CLS < 0.1, 60 fps.
